---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Builder from "../components/Builder";
---
<Base
  title="Create a repair completion report"
  description="A free form for a repair completion report. It flags what is missing or contradictory, then saves it as PDF or JSON. What you type stays in your browser."
  section="build"
  schema={{
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    name: "Open Repair Record builder",
    url: "https://openrepairrecord.com/build/",
    description:
      "A free form for one repair completion report. It checks what is missing or contradicts itself, then prints or saves the report as PDF or JSON. No account; everything runs in the browser.",
    applicationCategory: "BusinessApplication",
    operatingSystem: "Any (web browser)",
    browserRequirements: "Requires JavaScript",
    isAccessibleForFree: true,
    offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "EUR" },
  }}
>
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:32px">
    <div class="no-print" style="margin-bottom:20px">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.2rem);margin-bottom:6px">Create a repair completion report</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0;max-width:48rem">
        Fill in what you know. The check on the right tells you what is missing or contradicts itself. Your draft stays
        in this browser; nothing is uploaded.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Builder client:only="react">
      <p slot="fallback" class="muted">Loading the builder… It needs JavaScript; everything runs in your browser.</p>
    </Builder>

    <section class="prose no-print" style="margin-top:48px">
      <h2>What the report covers</h2>
      <p>
        A repair completion report written here keeps each source of information apart, so whoever reads it can tell
        what was claimed, what was checked, and what the resident said:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>What was reported:</strong> where, when, and the symptom in the reporter's words.</li>
        <li><strong>What the contractor says:</strong> what they did, the cause, and the outcome they report.</li>
        <li><strong>Checks:</strong> who checked, how, what they found, and what the check did not cover.</li>
        <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> photos, measurements, test logs or certificates, if any. Never required.</li>
        <li><strong>The resident:</strong> resolved, not resolved, not asked, waiting, no reply or not applicable.</li>
        <li><strong>Still open:</strong> anything left to do, with an owner and a date.</li>
        <li><strong>Closure:</strong> who closed the record, when, and why.</li>
        <li><strong>Later additions:</strong> a late reply, a revisit or a correction, added without rewriting.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Prefer paper? Print the <a href="/template/">blank repair completion report template</a>. New to this? Read
        <a href="/guide/">what "completed" should mean</a>, or start from one of the <a href="/examples/">worked examples</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
